{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-glossary-right-dual","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Remark","doco:Section"],"label":"rem:glossary-right-dual","kind":"remark","title":"Right dual","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-glossary-exact-pairing"],"tags":["glossary","category-theory","monoidal","duality"],"defines":["right-dual"],"text":"glossary-right-dual.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<p><a id=\"rem:glossary-right-dual\"></a>\n<strong>Remark.</strong> <em>Right dual</em></p>\n<p><strong><dfn class=\"defterm\" id=\"term-right-dual\">Right dual</dfn>.</strong> An object <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">X</code> in a monoidal category has a right dual if there exists an object <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">Y</code> and an exact pairing <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(X, Y)</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>Mathlib reference.</strong>\n<code>CategoryTheory.HasRightDual</code> (class).\nImport: <code>Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Monoidal.Rigid.Basic</code>.</p>\n"}
